WEBVTT

00:05.280 --> 00:07.190
Oh, I can't wait!

00:07.190 --> 00:11.780
Who'd have imagined that Lady Elise was 
hiding such outstanding abilities?

00:11.780 --> 00:15.460
I'm so looking forward to seeing her! 
Aren't you, Professor Graham?

00:15.460 --> 00:16.490
Yes.

00:17.100 --> 00:22.000
<i>If Lady Clorence truly did 
perform that treatment,</i>

00:22.790 --> 00:25.990
<i>then she may possess abilities 
equal to Rose's.</i>

00:31.070 --> 00:32.990
I must have fallen asleep.

00:33.950 --> 00:36.560
I wonder if Mil carried me to bed.

00:39.400 --> 00:42.550
My lady, there are visitors here to see you.

00:43.750 --> 00:45.630
Is it my brothers?

00:46.190 --> 00:47.350
Please, come in!

00:51.310 --> 00:52.350
Why?

00:53.130 --> 00:55.900
What are you doing here, Rose?

00:56.790 --> 00:59.610
D-Doctor Graham?

01:02.170 --> 01:04.850
<i>I never imagined I'd be 
exposed in such a manner!</i>

01:04.850 --> 01:07.340
<i>I can't explain this away!</i>

01:09.760 --> 01:13.630
I offer my deepest apologies 
for concealing my identity!

01:14.450 --> 01:18.380
I'm Elise de Clorence.

01:18.940 --> 01:21.130
So, it really is you.

01:21.500 --> 01:24.130
I thought you looked like her...

01:24.130 --> 01:26.910
but I never imagined that 
you actually <i>were</i> her!

01:28.880 --> 01:31.980
Now, let's set that aside. 
Please raise your head.

01:31.980 --> 01:34.760
We have good news for you today.

01:36.380 --> 01:39.670
We've come here after clearing up 
His Majesty's misunderstanding.

01:39.670 --> 01:43.950
We told him that your tracheotomy wasn't an 
act of disrespect toward the imperial family.

01:43.950 --> 01:46.660
Rather, it was a magnificent achievement!

01:49.010 --> 01:52.530
Why is your expression so somber?

01:52.530 --> 01:56.880
My lady, you've been declared innocent 
and you'll be able to leave this place!

01:57.280 --> 01:59.660
Th-Thank you.

02:03.770 --> 02:05.720
<i>Doctor Graham...</i>

02:05.720 --> 02:07.820
<i>He must be so shocked by this.</i>

03:45.990 --> 03:48.590
There are currently no 
issues with his heartbeat.

03:48.590 --> 03:51.490
We'll monitor his progress 
and administer medicine.

03:52.790 --> 03:57.250
Lady Clorence, is there something 
here which you find concerning?

03:57.720 --> 04:00.120
<i>H-He's speaking so formally!</i>

04:03.410 --> 04:06.300
Here is the report for the patient earlier.

04:06.300 --> 04:07.660
Thank you.

04:08.370 --> 04:12.510
Please feel free to speak without 
reserve, the way you did before.

04:12.830 --> 04:17.260
No, my lady. Our positions 
are too different.

04:21.700 --> 04:26.040
<i>Could it be that he's angry with 
me for concealing my identity?</i>

04:39.800 --> 04:42.310
<i>I'd like to explain my 
situation to him, but...</i>

04:43.670 --> 04:46.400
Yes! I understand. Thank you.

04:46.400 --> 04:49.330
Good. Right now, continuing the treatment 
is the most important thing.

04:49.330 --> 04:52.370
I understand. I'll continue 
it and keep monitoring.

04:50.370 --> 04:56.320
<i>After all, Doctor Graham is the only one 
here who knows I'm from the Clorence family.</i>

04:52.370 --> 04:55.210
I'm so glad I consulted you 
about this, Doctor Graham!

05:01.600 --> 05:02.500
Rose!

05:03.370 --> 05:05.070
I'm looking forward to working with you!

05:05.070 --> 05:05.960
What?

05:05.960 --> 05:07.900
Huh? Didn't you hear?

05:07.900 --> 05:10.670
Doctor Graham left work this morning,

05:10.670 --> 05:13.220
so you'll be with me for this 
afternoon's examinations.

05:13.220 --> 05:14.840
I-I see.

05:14.840 --> 05:16.370
Well, I'll see you later!

05:19.940 --> 05:23.460
<i>I suppose I'll speak with 
Doctor Graham tomorrow, then.</i>

05:24.870 --> 05:26.180
Excuse me.

05:26.180 --> 05:29.380
Have you seen Doctor Graham?

05:29.380 --> 05:32.230
Now that you mention it, 
I haven't seen him once.

05:32.550 --> 05:34.200
Perhaps he isn't in today.

05:47.170 --> 05:49.850
<i>Doctor Graham isn't here today either.</i>

05:52.090 --> 05:54.920
Um, is Doctor Graham...

05:57.050 --> 06:00.020
I heard he submitted a 
request for some leave.

06:00.020 --> 06:02.210
They say he'll be absent 
from work for a while.

06:02.880 --> 06:04.700
I see.

06:05.050 --> 06:07.910
But it's really unusual, you know?

06:07.910 --> 06:11.190
It's not like he's attending 
a big academic conference.

06:11.190 --> 06:14.720
And the day that he left work in the morning,

06:14.720 --> 06:17.110
he was acting a little strange, wasn't he?

06:17.110 --> 06:18.100
What?

06:18.420 --> 06:21.980
I learn a lot from doing the 
examinations with you, Rose,

06:21.980 --> 06:25.910
but when I have this many days go by without 
getting yelled at by Doctor Graham...

06:25.910 --> 06:29.620
I sort of lose motivation, you know?

06:30.100 --> 06:32.210
I wonder what's going on with him.

06:32.620 --> 06:34.870
Do you think something happened?

06:35.330 --> 06:37.760
<i>I'm certain this is my fault!</i>

06:44.680 --> 06:45.950
Thank you.

06:58.960 --> 07:00.310
Yes?

07:00.310 --> 07:03.890
I'm a student of Doctor 
Graham. My name is Rose.

07:03.890 --> 07:06.360
I was hoping to see him.

07:06.360 --> 07:08.290
Well, well. Welcome!

07:08.580 --> 07:11.140
I'm the nursemaid, Yodelle.

07:11.140 --> 07:13.250
Please, won't you come in?

07:13.250 --> 07:15.770
I will. Thank you so much!

07:21.430 --> 07:23.780
<i>He has so many books on medicine!</i>

07:24.510 --> 07:26.800
<i>And they've all been read so much.</i>

07:27.120 --> 07:31.000
<i>I can tell from every single one 
just how hard Doctor Graham works.</i>

07:31.000 --> 07:33.690
Miss Rose,

07:33.690 --> 07:35.810
please have some.

07:35.810 --> 07:37.310
Thank you!

07:42.800 --> 07:45.800
I tried calling the young master down,

07:45.800 --> 07:48.490
but he just won't leave his room.

07:48.490 --> 07:49.680
I see.

07:50.050 --> 07:52.520
He's been locked in there for days now.

07:54.470 --> 07:57.120
This sort of thing happens 
from time to time.

07:57.960 --> 08:00.890
He's been absent from the hospital 
for several days in a row.

08:00.890 --> 08:04.080
It isn't causing problems 
for everyone, is it?

08:04.080 --> 08:07.720
He applied for leave. 
Everything is just fine.

08:08.020 --> 08:09.920
That's all right, then.

08:09.920 --> 08:14.380
Oh, I know! I would love to know what the 
young master is like at the hospital!

08:14.380 --> 08:16.210
Won't you tell me?

08:16.690 --> 08:20.820
How does he spend his time? 
What sorts of things happen?

08:20.820 --> 08:24.220
He won't tell me anything at all, you see.

08:24.580 --> 08:27.470
Everyone adores Doctor Graham.

08:27.470 --> 08:28.740
Do they?

08:29.180 --> 08:32.190
Yes. His directions are always exact,

08:32.190 --> 08:34.230
so when any of the apprentice 
doctors have trouble

08:34.230 --> 08:38.390
they always go to consult 
Doctor Graham first!

08:40.510 --> 08:43.000
Everyone greatly depends on him.

08:43.000 --> 08:46.240
I'm so happy to hear that.

08:47.700 --> 08:49.390
You see, in the past...

08:52.010 --> 08:55.240
he would cry and cry every night.

08:55.240 --> 08:57.930
It was so difficult to help him fall asleep.

08:58.450 --> 09:00.690
<i>Doctor Graham was like that?</i>

09:00.690 --> 09:03.890
<i>Given the way he is now, 
I can't imagine that at all.</i>

09:05.040 --> 09:10.240
And now that same young master 
is a person everyone depends on.

09:10.240 --> 09:13.270
Oh, dear! I forgot to bring out 
snacks to go with the tea.

09:13.850 --> 09:15.400
I'll go and fetch some.

09:15.400 --> 09:16.180
Ow.

09:16.180 --> 09:17.280
Are you all right?

09:17.880 --> 09:21.580
Yes. I'm old, so I have 
pains here and there.

09:32.460 --> 09:34.200
What's wrong?

09:34.200 --> 09:35.800
I-It's nothing.

09:38.350 --> 09:39.670
Doctor Graham!

09:40.240 --> 09:43.160
Doctor! Doctor Graham!

09:45.530 --> 09:47.180
What's all the commotion?

09:50.910 --> 09:52.680
Doctor Graham...

09:53.760 --> 09:54.970
Yodelle!

10:00.410 --> 10:02.050
What happened to her?

10:02.050 --> 10:04.470
We were talking, then 
she suddenly collapsed!

10:05.660 --> 10:07.020
Does it hurt anywhere?

10:10.650 --> 10:13.200
She showed signs of pain in her abdomen.

10:23.990 --> 10:25.040
What is it?

10:25.040 --> 10:26.880
There's swelling in her groin.

10:28.980 --> 10:30.120
An abdominal hernia?

10:31.220 --> 10:33.100
It's hard and won't push backwards.

10:34.010 --> 10:36.320
An incarcerated inguinal hernia.

10:37.530 --> 10:41.320
Given the symptoms, necrosis of the 
intestine may have already begun!

10:42.430 --> 10:44.630
If we don't treat her immediately, it will cause

10:44.630 --> 10:47.330
intestinal perforation and 
inflammation of the abdominal lining.

10:47.330 --> 10:49.150
It could put her life at risk!

10:49.620 --> 10:52.110
Y-Young master!

10:55.640 --> 10:57.140
I'm sorry.

10:57.140 --> 10:58.950
This happened because I wasn't looking.

10:59.630 --> 11:00.620
Rose.

11:00.620 --> 11:01.380
Yes?

11:01.380 --> 11:03.910
As soon as we reach the hospital, 
I'll perform surgery.

11:03.910 --> 11:04.850
Please, help me.

11:04.850 --> 11:05.500
Yes, sir!

11:07.110 --> 11:09.020
Turn right at the next lane!

11:09.020 --> 11:10.440
That way is faster!

11:10.440 --> 11:11.170
Yes, sir!

11:18.770 --> 11:23.070
We will now begin a surgery 
to repair an inguinal hernia.

11:23.070 --> 11:23.870
Scalpel.

11:23.870 --> 11:24.400
Sir.

11:32.890 --> 11:33.950
Forceps.

11:36.900 --> 11:37.780
Here.

11:48.090 --> 11:49.250
Gauze.

11:50.970 --> 11:51.730
Here.

11:53.630 --> 11:55.000
<i>I will save you.</i>

11:56.120 --> 11:57.360
<i>There's just a little more!</i>

12:02.650 --> 12:04.100
Suturing complete.

12:11.130 --> 12:13.770
It finished without any problems. Thank you.

12:13.770 --> 12:14.240
Of course.

12:15.660 --> 12:18.520
I'm tired. We should rest a while.

12:18.520 --> 12:22.520
Then, I'll write up the operation report.

12:25.660 --> 12:29.130
After making an incision in the 
upper section of the hernia,

12:29.130 --> 12:33.500
we looked for a change in the color of the 
intestines and observed the blood flow.

12:41.610 --> 12:42.940
I'll write it.

12:42.940 --> 12:43.620
What?

12:53.020 --> 12:56.390
By the way, what brought 
you to my house today?

12:56.870 --> 12:58.780
I went to apologize.

12:59.130 --> 13:02.480
You were angry that I concealed my identity.

13:02.480 --> 13:05.300
That's why you asked for 
several days leave, isn't it?

13:06.520 --> 13:07.560
Angry?

13:07.910 --> 13:09.100
Yes.

13:09.100 --> 13:11.460
In your office, you...

13:11.460 --> 13:15.550
you drew your eyebrows together 
and sighed heavily, didn't you?

13:15.550 --> 13:16.900
Sighed?

13:17.420 --> 13:18.810
Oh, right.

13:19.220 --> 13:20.560
That was because...

13:21.100 --> 13:23.460
I was shocked at your 
handwriting, that's all.

13:23.790 --> 13:27.060
It's so bad that it takes a 
long time to read, you see.

13:28.450 --> 13:30.980
S-So that's what it was.

13:30.980 --> 13:33.360
What sort of misunderstanding is that?

13:33.360 --> 13:36.470
I wanted to focus on my research, 
so I took some time off, that's all.

13:37.940 --> 13:39.970
You're the one who gave 
me the push to do it.

13:40.710 --> 13:41.840
I did?

13:41.840 --> 13:42.680
Yes.

13:43.200 --> 13:45.400
You're always working your hardest, right?

13:46.650 --> 13:49.520
Remember the hospital wing 
I first took you to?

13:50.320 --> 13:54.470
Even within the hospital, they say 
that's the cruelest of places.

13:55.190 --> 13:59.220
When you saw the filthy conditions, 
I thought you'd run right away,

14:00.010 --> 14:01.640
but you didn't.

14:03.210 --> 14:05.860
Hiding your identity while 
aiming to become a doctor...

14:06.150 --> 14:08.500
Studying on your own to 
learn medical science...

14:08.500 --> 14:10.320
neither of those paths are an easy one.

14:10.750 --> 14:13.240
I want to learn that 
strength of will from you.

14:13.690 --> 14:15.770
Oh, no. It isn't anything so grand.

14:15.770 --> 14:17.370
And your skills are sound, too.

14:17.370 --> 14:18.320
What?

14:19.280 --> 14:21.870
Treatment of the patient with 
the tension pneumothorax...

14:22.930 --> 14:24.420
the splenectomy...

14:26.650 --> 14:28.950
even the tracheotomy you 
performed the other day...

14:28.950 --> 14:30.830
Only you could have done all that.

14:31.690 --> 14:33.330
I'm not capable of it.

14:33.330 --> 14:35.500
Though I studied so hard at the academy,

14:35.500 --> 14:38.110
and I've read all the
 medical texts over and over...

14:38.760 --> 14:41.370
People around me say that 
I have a talent for this,

14:41.980 --> 14:44.870
but I'm no more than an average 
person who works my very hardest.

14:45.650 --> 14:48.620
But you have a talent you were born with.

14:49.520 --> 14:51.590
To be honest, I'm jealous.

14:52.200 --> 14:55.120
I think that the emotions 
I feel toward you...

14:55.760 --> 14:57.860
are envy and respect.

14:59.780 --> 15:01.520
I'm certain I feel them both.

15:05.690 --> 15:09.130
Doctor, why did you decide to 
decide to become a physician?

15:12.170 --> 15:14.160
Because I lost my family.

15:14.900 --> 15:15.650
What?

15:16.730 --> 15:18.160
Twenty years ago.

15:20.320 --> 15:25.240
I had my parents, an older 
brother, and an older sister.

15:25.240 --> 15:29.390
And I also had an adorable little brother.

15:30.560 --> 15:32.660
Mama, look! Look!

15:34.420 --> 15:36.480
It's a clover of happiness!

15:45.270 --> 15:47.850
Papa! There are so many dolphins!

15:54.530 --> 15:57.800
Every single day was a happy one.

16:05.040 --> 16:06.110
But...

16:06.950 --> 16:09.320
Don't take them away!

16:09.320 --> 16:10.940
Young master, you mustn't!

16:11.340 --> 16:15.990
A hundred and fifty thousand people 
died in the Laurage epidemic.

16:15.990 --> 16:17.930
My family was infected, too.

16:23.620 --> 16:24.960
When they were on the verge of death...

16:26.080 --> 16:28.470
I couldn't even sit by their sides.

16:38.480 --> 16:40.500
But what about the young master?

16:40.500 --> 16:45.220
He can't pay us, and we have our 
livelihoods to worry about...

16:48.390 --> 16:52.600
Disease stole everything that I held dear.

16:59.300 --> 17:01.230
I was a ruined noble.

17:01.740 --> 17:04.280
The only person to hold 
out their hand to me...

17:04.950 --> 17:06.260
was Yodelle.

17:07.760 --> 17:11.870
She was like family to me.

17:14.310 --> 17:18.750
There was a time when Yodelle fell ill.

17:24.660 --> 17:26.290
That's when I had the thought...

17:27.420 --> 17:31.790
I wasn't going to let disease steal 
anything precious to me ever again.

17:32.550 --> 17:36.310
My family's deaths, the presence 
of someone important to me...

17:37.240 --> 17:40.030
those things gave me the 
determination to become a doctor.

17:44.260 --> 17:45.560
Doctor.

17:45.560 --> 17:46.290
What is it?

17:47.140 --> 17:50.180
I hold your hard work in the highest regard.

17:53.130 --> 17:54.270
Thank you.

18:00.820 --> 18:02.310
How beautiful!

18:21.920 --> 18:24.190
Oh, that's right! Doctor Graham?

18:25.470 --> 18:29.720
Please call me Rose, not Lady Clorence.

18:29.720 --> 18:32.490
After all, I'm your apprentice!

18:32.490 --> 18:34.330
R-Right.

18:46.010 --> 18:47.920
What am I feeling embarrassed about?

19:01.080 --> 19:02.060
Lise!

19:02.790 --> 19:04.190
Lise!

19:04.190 --> 19:08.200
Congratulations! You're going to be 
awarded the Order of the Imperial Rose!

19:08.200 --> 19:09.230
What?

19:10.030 --> 19:12.280
The Order of the Imperial Rose?

19:13.220 --> 19:15.740
This is no time to stand around in a daze!

19:15.740 --> 19:18.470
Your tracheotomy has been 
accepted and acknowledged!

19:18.470 --> 19:21.620
To think you'd be awarded 
such a prestigious title!

19:21.620 --> 19:23.390
I-I can't breathe.

19:31.570 --> 19:32.770
Young master?

19:33.210 --> 19:34.780
Are you feeling any pain anywhere?

19:35.220 --> 19:40.490
No. I'm terribly sorry to have worried you.

19:41.440 --> 19:43.810
It's my fault for not noticing.

19:44.370 --> 19:47.230
But you have to tell me when 
you're not feeling well.

19:47.740 --> 19:48.510
Yes.

19:49.590 --> 19:51.370
Because we're family.

19:53.040 --> 19:54.120
Yes!

19:58.480 --> 20:00.070
What are you doing?

20:04.350 --> 20:07.230
I'm happy to be back
 to the regular routine.

20:07.230 --> 20:08.130
What?

20:08.470 --> 20:11.140
I hadn't been scolded by you for a few days,

20:11.140 --> 20:13.140
so everything felt a little empty.

20:13.440 --> 20:14.890
What is that supposed to mean?

20:15.440 --> 20:16.380
There you are!

20:17.900 --> 20:19.080
Over here! Over here!

20:19.750 --> 20:22.460
Doctor, there's something 
I wanted to consult about.

20:22.460 --> 20:24.290
Will you come to the office with us?

20:24.690 --> 20:25.480
Of course.

20:26.020 --> 20:27.750
Then, I'll see you later.

20:27.750 --> 20:29.150
Yes, young master.

20:29.150 --> 20:31.060
Doctor, hurry up!

20:31.060 --> 20:32.170
I'm coming.

20:33.920 --> 20:35.030
Isn't this great?

20:35.030 --> 20:37.560
Yes. I really wanted Doctor 
Graham's advice on this.

22:06.260 --> 22:09.970
Days Long Ago
